77\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.006137272963921229, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/permutations.cc\"], \"retained\": [\"Format independent character/space pairs using guarded 16-byte and 8-byte NEON operations, with a scalar remainder and portable fallback.\", \"Accumulate ordered output in a fixed 64 KiB buffer instead of performing per-character stream insertions and per-permutation flushes.\", \"Keep the permutation in a conventional string and use sequential std::next_permutation for safe termination without decrementing before begin.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"f42243bc26114949\", \"role\": \"B\", \"commit\": \"8ec6957aedd7770e27406083450a0d9086cf8e7b\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.006217746064066887, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/permutations.cc\"], \"retained\": [\"Copy each formatted record into an uncommitted buffer slot, then update only symbol positions using the lexicographic successor algorithm.\", \"Use NEON copies between disjoint records without overreading or overwriting record boundaries; preserve the last record across buffer flushes.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"53f594bb09e8489c\", \"role\": \"C\", \"commit\": \"ed6c3a3a41096fefbd9afdfd7baff953b2e83153\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.0062416062379876775, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/permutations.cc\"], \"retained\": [\"Partition enumeration into unique lexicographic prefix subtrees using overflow-safe, capped multiset counts.\", \"Dynamically schedule coarse tasks within one persistent OpenMP team.\", \"Serialize output in lexicographic waves of at most 16 tasks, each emitting at most 256 KiB.\", \"Preserve exact whitespace filtering and output bytes while buffering sequential output and retaining a general fallback.\"]}}, {\"id\": \"247e125b38d94513\", \"role\": \"C\", \"commit\": \"04e863a312717744d4a3e3706cd49edeeaca7d97\", \"mean_seconds\": 0.006512396037578583, \"transformations\": {\"files\": [\"src/permutations.cc\"], \"retained\": [\"Replace per-permutation flushing with bounded buffered output.\", \"Com